      "text": "My goodness, I never noticed a thing! On our first day we visited the legendary Raffles Hotel from the 19th century, the very difinition of British Colonial. Then St. Andrew's Anglican Chuch, built in 1827. On to the Sri Mariamman Hindu Temple, built in 1827. After that, I now realise, everything was 'reclaimed (manufactured)' land! The whole business district of sky scrapers, the forests of orderly apartment blocks, the airport, the trains, Marina Bay, the hotel with the stranded ship, the Lotus - all manufactured. My my, I didn't notice a thing. Ironic that the products of the refinery will indirectly threaten the country through fossil fuel burning -> greenhouse gases -> further warming of earth -> further rising of sea level.",
      "likeCount": 0,
      "publishedAt": "2026-09-09T11:39:52Z",
      "replyCount": 1,
      "replies": [
        {
          "id": "UgyaOLW3jWf9ZXym_dh4AaABAg.AaXg37ebHdrAa_JSEylibY",
